                      \n                                        $y(\\frac{3}{2})≈$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $\\frac{93}{16}$\n\nEarlier part 5:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to 1}\\frac{y(x)-2}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x)}=$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-\\frac{4}{\\pi}$\n\nCurrent part:\n\nFind the general solution to the differential equation ${y}^{′}=x{y}^{2}.$ Assume that $y\\ne 0$ and $K$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $y=-2($ \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $+K)^{-1}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039183/state.json" "file_sha256" "e63a19903454870345cc479d4734f172538a39d1bb775ef7cec23c3e76790211"} {"question" "q-128191" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =x{y}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -\\frac{1}{y} & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we solve for $y.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{y} & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+C \\\\ -\\frac{1}{y} & =\\frac{{x}^{2}+2C}{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{y} & =-\\frac{{x}^{2}+2C}{2} \\\\ y & =-\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}+2C} \\\\ y & =-\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}+K} \\\\ y & =-2{({x}^{2}+K)}^{-1},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K=2C$ is an arbitrary constant." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039183/state.json" "file_sha256" "e63a19903454870345cc479d4734f172538a39d1bb775ef7cec23c3e76790211"} {"question" "q-128191" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039183/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ddd149e61113f0ba9be0dc932e525b10c73bcb40bf913ff8069c0906fb9584fc"} {"question" "q-128191" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039183/state.json" "file_sha256" "e63a19903454870345cc479d4734f172538a39d1bb775ef7cec23c3e76790211"} {"question" "q-128191" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x^2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039183/state.json" "file_sha256" "e63a19903454870345cc479d4734f172538a39d1bb775ef7cec23c3e76790211"} {"question" "q-128192" "field" nil "attribute" "que